            <div xml:id="d609">

                <pb facs="0690" n="678" sameAs="frus:frus1943v02/pg678"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">852.6363/805: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Hayes</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-04-30T12:00:00+02:00">April 30,
                            1943—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 2:43 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1098. In exercise of the discretion given to me in your 970, April 29, 11 p.m.
                        [<hi rendition="#italic">a.m.</hi>] I have authorized sailings proposed in
                    my 1086, April 29, 2 p.m.<anchor n="21" xml:id="d609-f1"/> I am prepared to
                    justify to the President my decision in this regard which has been made in the
                    light of the President’s approval of our petroleum program and the relation of
                    that program to our entire policy toward Spain which is bringing results of
                    incalculable benefit to our war effort.</p>
                <p>In a subsequent telegram I shall outline my views in response to Department’s
                    958, April 27, 3 p.m. I request no categoric instructions limiting sailings or
                    loadings of Spanish tankers be issued prior to receipt and consideration of that
                    telegram.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hayes</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
